[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660325025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102398#issuecomment-2660325025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102398","id":2660325025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ekVah","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-14T21:41:54Z","updated_at":"2025-02-14T21:41:54Z","body":"> Can signals for fade be added to this?\r\n\r\nI can add an explicit signal for this but my thinking was that unlike in the blend tree case there will always be a `state_started` or `state_finished` signal when crossfade starts or ends. If an additional signal is preferred, would it be better to adopt the same generic signal with an enum approach?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660325025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660561477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102398#issuecomment-2660561477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102398","id":2660561477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6elPJF","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T00:21:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T00:21:56Z","body":"@a-johnston Ah, so you are saying that in this PR, the start of the fade is the next state's `state_started` and the end of the fade is the previous state's `state_finished`. Indeed, it sounds reasonable, so in that case the signal about fading may not be necessary.\r\n\r\nHowever, I am concerned about what happens when the fade is interrupted or the StateMachine itself is interrupted. So we will need to test this in detail later when we do a proper review. For example, we should have some test cases to see if the two states (fading from state & current state) correctly fire the `state_finished` signal when a restart occurs during a fade.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660561477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781106478","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102398#issuecomment-2781106478","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102398","id":2781106478,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lxFEu","user":{"login":"catprisbrey","id":43008564,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMDA4NTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43008564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey","html_url":"https://github.com/catprisbrey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catprisbrey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-05T21:49:49Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T21:49:49Z","body":"I've got to say, following this ticket progress these past months. I'm extremely excited for when this gets added. I have several odd workarounds going on now that will immediately be solved by this node signaler once it's available. Thank you so so so much each of you who has taken steps to progress it and keep it moving forward. I'm very grateful!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"